 ## Background
-NerfTree, also known as Efficient-NeRF, was introduced by Hyan et al. [HLC* 22] as part of the broader effort to make NeRF training and rendering more efficient. It builds upon multistage, coarse-to-fine strategies adopted by works like TNSVF [LGZL* 20] and others [SSC22, YLT* 21], but specifically implements a two-level octree structure. The method is inspired by classical computer graphics techniques such as the Bounding Volume Hierarchy (BVH) [RW80] and the Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) [LK10], which model scenes in a sparse hierarchical form to accelerate ray tracing [S1].
